# ⚙️ How It Works

### Step 1 — Sensor Monitoring

Each ESP32 continuously reads sensor values.

```text
PIR
 ↓
Vibration
 ↓
Tamper
 ↓
Device Health
```

### Step 2 — Local Processing

The ESP32 performs basic threshold/rule checks.

Example:

```text
Motion = TRUE
Vibration = FALSE
Tamper = FALSE
```

### Step 3 — Send Data

The node publishes data through MQTT.

Example:

```json
{
  "deviceId": "NODE-003",
  "zone": "ZONE-C",
  "motion": true,
  "vibration": false,
  "tamper": false,
  "battery": 87,
  "timestamp": "2026-08-19T02:35:21Z"
}
```

### Step 4 — Backend Processing

The backend receives the sensor event and determines the event status.

```text
NORMAL
WARNING
ALERT
```

### Step 5 — Dashboard

The event is displayed on the monitoring dashboard.

```text
┌───────────────────────────────────┐
│     PERIMETER MONITORING          │
├───────────────────────────────────┤
│ Zone A     🟢 NORMAL              │
│ Zone B     🟢 NORMAL              │
│ Zone C     🔴 ALERT               │
│ Zone D     🟡 WARNING             │
└───────────────────────────────────┘
```

